select 'c768e8c0-d0a0-557f-8467-eb1b1d7d715a', e.id, 'IN', (select id from public.content_components where code = 'IN.P6'), 'qa_passed', 'cefr_part', '{"title":"Why we forget what we study","text":"Most students have had this experience: you study for hours the night before a test, you feel ready, and a week later you can hardly remember anything. This is not because you are lazy or because your memory is bad. It is simply how the brain works.\n\nMore than a hundred years ago, the German psychologist Hermann Ebbinghaus tested his own memory by learning lists of invented words. He discovered that we forget new information very quickly at first, and then more slowly. He called this pattern the \"forgetting curve\".\n\nThe good news is that the curve can be changed. Every time we try to remember something, especially just before we forget it, the memory becomes stronger and lasts longer. This is why reviewing material several times over days or weeks works much better than reading it many times in one evening. Testing yourself is also more effective than simply rereading your notes, because it forces your brain to bring the information back.\n\nOf course, these techniques require planning. You cannot leave everything until the last night. But students who space out their studying usually find that they need less total time, and that they remember more months later.","svg":null,"table":null}'::jsonb, 'According to the text, when is it especially useful to try to remember something?', '[{"label":"A","text":"Only on the night before the test.","is_correct":false,"distractor_type":"Contradice la recomendación del texto.","explanation_feedback":"Incorrecta. El texto critica dejar todo para la última noche."},{"label":"B","text":"Just before you are about to forget it.","is_correct":true,"distractor_type":null,"explanation_feedback":"Correcta. El texto dice que el recuerdo se fortalece sobre todo si se intenta «just before we forget it»."},{"label":"C","text":"Immediately after you have learned it.","is_correct":false,"distractor_type":"Supone que repasar enseguida es lo mejor.","explanation_feedback":"Incorrecta. El texto destaca el momento justo antes de olvidar, no inmediatamente después."},{"label":"D","text":"When you have read it many times.","is_correct":false,"distractor_type":"Confunde releer con recuperar.","explanation_feedback":"Incorrecta. Releer muchas veces en una tarde es justo lo que el texto considera menos eficaz."}]'::jsonb, 'B1', 1.3, 1.3, 0.25, 90, 'original_generated'
