select '04130038-698d-5aeb-842d-535ed2194ecb', e.id, 'IN', (select id from public.content_components where code = 'IN.P6'), 'qa_passed', 'cefr_part', '{"title":"Why we forget what we study","text":"Most students have had this experience: you study for hours the night before a test, you feel ready, and a week later you can hardly remember anything. This is not because you are lazy or because your memory is bad. It is simply how the brain works.\n\nMore than a hundred years ago, the German psychologist Hermann Ebbinghaus tested his own memory by learning lists of invented words. He discovered that we forget new information very quickly at first, and then more slowly. He called this pattern the \"forgetting curve\".\n\nThe good news is that the curve can be changed. Every time we try to remember something, especially just before we forget it, the memory becomes stronger and lasts longer. This is why reviewing material several times over days or weeks works much better than reading it many times in one evening. Testing yourself is also more effective than simply rereading your notes, because it forces your brain to bring the information back.\n\nOf course, these techniques require planning. You cannot leave everything until the last night. But students who space out their studying usually find that they need less total time, and that they remember more months later.","svg":null,"table":null}'::jsonb, 'Why is testing yourself better than rereading your notes?', '[{"label":"A","text":"Your notes usually have many mistakes.","is_correct":false,"distractor_type":"Inventa una razón.","explanation_feedback":"Incorrecta. El texto no dice que los apuntes tengan errores."},{"label":"B","text":"Teachers prefer students who test themselves.","is_correct":false,"distractor_type":"Inventa una razón externa.","explanation_feedback":"Incorrecta. El texto no habla de lo que prefieren los profesores."},{"label":"C","text":"It takes less time than reading your notes.","is_correct":false,"distractor_type":"Supone una ventaja de tiempo no mencionada en esa parte.","explanation_feedback":"Incorrecta. La razón dada es que obliga al cerebro a recuperar, no que tome menos tiempo."},{"label":"D","text":"It makes the brain bring information back from memory.","is_correct":true,"distractor_type":null,"explanation_feedback":"Correcta. Al autoevaluarte obligas al cerebro a recuperar la información, y eso la fortalece."}]'::jsonb, 'B1', 1.3, 1.3, 0.25, 90, 'original_generated'
